# Local build output — must never land in a build context. Without this, a locally-built
# src/**/obj/project.assets.json gets copied over the container's own fresh `dotnet restore`
# output, and `dotnet publish --no-restore` fails claiming a package "was not found" even though
# restore just succeeded (NETSDK1064) — the obj/ folder it reads from is the wrong one.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.vs/
.vscode/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
